# A play-by-mail game, first turn: the 1942 scenario, UTILITY, Begin PBM. The game becomes a
# two-player game on the Allied side. Esc at the PBM Drive menu keeps the drive of ww2.cfg, which
# is "" here, so the PBM file is "pbm" in the game's folder. The drive menu's first entry is
# LEFT$(CURDIR$, 2), which differs from machine to machine, so no digest is taken while it shows.
# The Allied side recruits twice in Birmingham, then ends its turn: the game writes the PBM file,
# shows "PBM File has been saved" and ends. The file is the start of pbm-1942-axis
# (tests/data/pbm/1942-axis.pbm).
#! seed 1942
#! files pbm

rule 1 key space

# The title menu: Start NEW Game. Start Year: 1942, the fourth entry.
play until 2:W
text s
play until 2:S
key down
prompt
key down
prompt
key down
prompt
key enter

# UTILITY: Begin PBM is the fourth entry from the end (PgDn, then Up three times).
play until 2:M
digest
text u
prompt
key pagedown
prompt
key up
prompt
key up
prompt
key up
prompt
digest
key enter
# The PBM Drive menu: Esc.
prompt
key esc

# Recruit: Birmingham twice, then Esc.
play until 2:M
digest
text r
prompt
digest
key enter
prompt
key enter
prompt
digest
key esc

# END TURN, Yes: the PBM file is written, and the game ends at "press a key".
play until 2:M
digest
text e
play until 2:E
text y
play until 1
digest
repeat space
